Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
12. Exchange model: compare g, Delta and L using resolved spectral statistics\
\>", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"aaef69b0-aab8-7d40-815d-4935ae7f6e0d"],

Cell["\<\
This chapter adds the comparison proposal that was previously missing from \
the .m file. The coupling scales below are distinct from each other. The \
gap-ratio cells can analyze the existing exchange sweep without \
rediagonalizing it. They do not automatically perform the proposed multi-size \
scan or establish a fitted crossover law.
Write H(g)=H0+gV, where H0 is the middle XXZ chain and two free edge spins, \
and V=edgeBonds[exUsed][\"Exchange\"] is dimensionless. Each edge bond has \
norm |g|/2 in the S=sigma/2 convention; the two-bond perturbation has norm at \
most |g|. For Delta=0 the full exchange model is a free-fermion chain for all \
g. For interacting Delta, generic boundary exchange can break integrability, \
but remaining symmetries must first be resolved and exceptional points must \
be checked. The absence of a paper's tuning relations alone is not a proof of \
nonintegrability.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"26f522b9-3058-114a-9414-6fe428516510"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["12.1 Three comparisons; no single ratio diagnoses chaos", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"92a24aa0-7b64-ea47-9388-e4b995944499"],

Cell["\<\
(1) Microscopic comparison: lambda=|g|/|J|. This compares the edge exchange \
coefficient with the transverse bulk exchange coefficient. The actual edge \
flip-flop matrix element is g/2, and the longitudinal bulk coefficient is J \
Delta. Keep Delta and the sign of J explicit when comparing different runs.
(2) Nearby-level hybridization: Lambda_nm=|g <n|V|m>|/|E_n^(0)-E_m^(0)|, \
within the same compatible symmetry sector and spectral window. Both the \
matrix elements and the spacings depend on L and Delta. A window-averaged |g| \
v_typ/d_typ can summarize this after defining how the matrix-element and \
spacing samples are selected. Comparing g with the mean level spacing alone \
neglects selection rules and matrix-element size. At g=0, first diagonalize V \
inside each exactly degenerate H0 manifold; never divide by a zero spacing. \
If an uncoupled pair has a vanishing matrix element, its small spacing does \
not imply hybridization.
(3) Low-energy comparison: kappa=|g|/epsilon_op(L,Delta), where epsilon_op is \
a positive bulk excitation energy accessible from the chosen low-energy state \
through the boundary operators S_2^+/- or S_(L-1)^+/-. Treat any degenerate \
ground manifold separately. In the gapless bulk the finite-size low-energy \
scales are typically of order v(Delta)/(L-2), with corrections; in the gapped \
bulk accessible bulk excitations can retain a finite scale. Boundary modes \
and nearly degenerate vacua must not be substituted automatically for the \
bulk gap. This low-energy comparison addresses boundary response and differs \
from spectral mixing in the central many-body band.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"bd4fc7f2-d9cf-e546-80b9-62d53d35830e"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["12.2 Concrete finite-size spectral comparison", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"34543461-6dc4-0147-a404-a0de51e7ef88"],

Cell["\<\
Proposal: for antiferromagnetic J>0, compare L={8,10,12}, extending to L=14 \
when feasible, and Delta={0,0.5,1,1.5,3}. Use a common dimensionless lambda \
grid, initially logarithmic over positive lambda, with an explicitly separate \
g=0 endpoint. Refine the grid where the statistics change; no interpolation \
is needed to display the measured samples.
For even L, use (m=0,R=+1,F=+1) as the primary sector and analyze other \
sectors independently as checks. Its dimension is only 23 at L=8, so that \
size is indicative. Never pool equal-spectrum partners or sectors with \
different parities. Start with the middle 50 percent of ranks in each sector \
and record the actual level and ratio counts. This rank window is an \
operational convention, not an identical energy density across all L and \
Delta; check an energy-density window if a quantitative size collapse is \
pursued.
Compute delta_n=E_(n+1)-E_n and \
rtilde_n=Min[delta_n,delta_(n+1)]/Max[delta_n,delta_(n+1)] from unchopped \
energies. The reference means are 2 Log[2]-1=0.386294... for Poisson and \
approximately 0.5307 for a large GOE ensemble; the GOE three-level surmise \
gives a slightly different 0.5359. No unfolding is required for this ratio. \
Reference [2]: Y. Y. Atas et al., Phys. Rev. Lett. 110, 084101 (2013): \
https://arxiv.org/abs/1212.5611 .
Plot mean rtilde versus g/|J| separately for each L,Delta. If the data \
support a crossover, a crossing of the midpoint (0.3863+0.5307)/2=0.4585 can \
be reported descriptively only after checking size, window, gap resolution \
and uncertainty stability. A raw first crossing on a dense correlated g grid \
is not a reliable crossover estimator. Do not assume monotonicity or fit a \
size exponent before observing the curves. Boundary-only perturbations need \
not follow scaling laws derived for extensive bulk perturbations.
Controls: exchange at Delta=0, and the integrable ZZ model in separately \
resolved actual sectors. Integrability does not guarantee Poisson statistics \
for very small sectors or spectra with extra degeneracies. The g=0 free-edge \
spectrum requires endpoint refinements. For any unresolved or zero gap, \
report it; do not silently remove levels.
Reference [3] for the motivating boundary-impurity setting: P. Kattel et al., \
Edge modes and boundary impurities in the anisotropic Heisenberg spin chain, \
section V and appendix C: https://arxiv.org/abs/2412.00194 . Its \
nonintegrable study motivates comparison; it is not a direct verification of \
our XY-only two-edge path or its finite-size crossover.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"0427e18c-a015-1648-b47b-d54d6d19fef4"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["12.3 Gap-ratio definitions using retained exchange data", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"195fed95-b87c-b74a-b843-541132f3f8e7"],

Cell["\<\
The following functions keep every input energy, use a tolerance only to FLAG \
unresolved gaps, and return Missing for the sector mean if any gap pair in \
the chosen window is unresolved. Counts and individual ratio entries are \
retained. At g=0, exGapRows returns a separate DecoupledEndpoint status \
because the stored parent energies recombine extra symmetry sectors. The \
plotting helper omits Missing means, states the number of omitted samples, \
and leaves every status in the diagnostics table. It never joins points. \
These cells require the unchanged plotting definitions from section 2.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"440d8340-bfc3-9a42-b0fa-ff659e02ca98"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"ClearAll", "[", 
   RowBox[{"exGapRatios", ",", "exGapRows", ",", "exRatioPanel"}], "]"}], 
  ";"}]], "Input",ExpressionUUID->"09348e9a-f39d-8540-befd-24f3bff4fa3f"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"(*", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"Raw", " ", "levels", " ", 
     RowBox[{"only", ":", " ", 
      RowBox[{"no", " ", "Chop"}]}]}], ",", " ", "unfolding", ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"or", " ", "removal", " ", "of", " ", "degenerate", " ", 
     RowBox[{"levels", "."}]}]}], " ", "*)"}], "\n", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"exGapRatios", "[", 
     RowBox[{"energies_List", ",", 
      RowBox[{"window_", ":", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"1", "/", "4"}], ",", 
         RowBox[{"3", "/", "4"}]}], "}"}]}], ",", 
      RowBox[{"tol_", ":", 
       RowBox[{"10", "^", 
        RowBox[{"-", "10"}]}]}]}], "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
    RowBox[{"Module", "[", "\n", " ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"e", "=", 
         RowBox[{"Sort", "[", 
          RowBox[{"N", "[", "energies", "]"}], "]"}]}], ",", "d", ",", "lo", ",",
         "hi", ",", "w", ",", "gaps", ",", "cut", ",", "pairs", ",", "ratios",
         ",", "unresolved", ",", "status"}], "}"}], ",", "\n", " ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"check", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"AllTrue", "[", 
           RowBox[{"e", ",", "realQ"}], "]"}], " ", "&&", " ", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"Length", "[", "window", "]"}], "==", "2"}], " ", "&&", 
          " ", 
          RowBox[{"0", "<=", 
           RowBox[{"window", "[", 
            RowBox[{"[", "1", "]"}], "]"}], "<", 
           RowBox[{"window", "[", 
            RowBox[{"[", "2", "]"}], "]"}], "<=", "1"}], " ", "&&", "\n", 
          "  ", 
          RowBox[{"realQ", "[", "tol", "]"}], " ", "&&", " ", 
          RowBox[{"tol", ">", "0"}]}], 
         ",", "\"\<Invalid energy list, rank window, or gap tolerance.\>\""}],
         "]"}], ";", "\n", " ", 
       RowBox[{"d", "=", 
        RowBox[{"Length", "[", "e", "]"}]}], ";", 
       RowBox[{"lo", "=", 
        RowBox[{"Max", "[", 
         RowBox[{"1", ",", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"Floor", "[", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"window", "[", 
              RowBox[{"[", "1", "]"}], "]"}], " ", "d"}], "]"}], "+", "1"}]}],
          "]"}]}], ";", 
       RowBox[{"hi", "=", 
        RowBox[{"Min", "[", 
         RowBox[{"d", ",", 
          RowBox[{"Ceiling", "[", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"window", "[", 
             RowBox[{"[", "2", "]"}], "]"}], " ", "d"}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], ";",
        "\n", " ", 
       RowBox[{"w", "=", 
        RowBox[{"If", "[", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"d", ">", "0"}], " ", "&&", " ", 
           RowBox[{"hi", ">=", "lo"}]}], ",", 
          RowBox[{"e", "[", 
           RowBox[{"[", 
            RowBox[{"lo", ";;", "hi"}], "]"}], "]"}], ",", 
          RowBox[{"{", "}"}]}], "]"}]}], ";", 
       RowBox[{"gaps", "=", 
        RowBox[{"Differences", "[", "w", "]"}]}], ";", "\n", " ", 
       RowBox[{"cut", "=", 
        RowBox[{"tol", " ", 
         RowBox[{"Max", "[", 
          RowBox[{"1.", ",", 
           RowBox[{"maxAbs", "[", "e", "]"}]}], "]"}]}]}], ";", 
       RowBox[{"pairs", "=", 
        RowBox[{"Partition", "[", 
         RowBox[{"gaps", ",", "2", ",", "1"}], "]"}]}], ";", "\n", " ", 
       RowBox[{"ratios", "=", 
        RowBox[{"Map", "[", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"If", "[", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{"Min", "[", "#", "]"}], "<=", "cut"}], ",", 
             RowBox[{"Missing", "[", "\"\<UnresolvedGapPair\>\"", "]"}], ",", 
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{"Min", "[", "#", "]"}], "/", 
              RowBox[{"Max", "[", "#", "]"}]}]}], "]"}], "&"}], ",", 
          "pairs"}], "]"}]}], ";", "\n", " ", 
       RowBox[{"unresolved", "=", 
        RowBox[{"Count", "[", 
         RowBox[{"ratios", ",", "_Missing"}], "]"}]}], ";", "\n", " ", 
       RowBox[{"status", "=", 
        RowBox[{"Which", "[", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"Length", "[", "w", "]"}], "<", "3"}], 
          ",", "\"\<TooFewLevels\>\"", ",", 
          RowBox[{"unresolved", ">", "0"}], ",", "\"\<UnresolvedGaps\>\"", ",",
           "True", ",", "\"\<OK\>\""}], "]"}]}], ";", "\n", " ", 
       RowBox[{"<|", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"\"\<SectorDimension\>\"", "->", "d"}], ",", 
         RowBox[{"\"\<WindowRanks\>\"", "->", 
          RowBox[{"{", 
           RowBox[{"lo", ",", "hi"}], "}"}]}], ",", 
         RowBox[{"\"\<WindowLevels\>\"", "->", 
          RowBox[{"Length", "[", "w", "]"}]}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
         RowBox[{"\"\<GapPairs\>\"", "->", 
          RowBox[{"Length", "[", "pairs", "]"}]}], ",", 
         RowBox[{"\"\<UnresolvedGapPairs\>\"", "->", "unresolved"}], ",", 
         "\n", "  ", 
         RowBox[{"\"\<UnresolvedGaps\>\"", "->", 
          RowBox[{"Count", "[", 
           RowBox[{"gaps", ",", 
            RowBox[{"x_", "/;", 
             RowBox[{"x", "<=", "cut"}]}]}], "]"}]}], ",", 
         RowBox[{"\"\<GapResolution\>\"", "->", "cut"}], ",", "\n", "  ", 
         RowBox[{"\"\<Ratios\>\"", "->", "ratios"}], ",", 
         RowBox[{"\"\<MeanR\>\"", "->", 
          RowBox[{"If", "[", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"status", "==", "\"\<OK\>\""}], ",", 
            RowBox[{"Mean", "[", "ratios", "]"}], ",", 
            RowBox[{"Missing", "[", "status", "]"}]}], "]"}]}], ",", "\n", 
         "  ", 
         RowBox[{"\"\<IIDSEM\>\"", "->", 
          RowBox[{"If", "[", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"status", "==", "\"\<OK\>\""}], " ", "&&", " ", 
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{"Length", "[", "ratios", "]"}], ">=", "2"}]}], ",", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"StandardDeviation", "[", "ratios", "]"}], "/", 
             RowBox[{"Sqrt", "[", 
              RowBox[{"Length", "[", "ratios", "]"}], "]"}]}], ",", 
            RowBox[{"Missing", "[", "\"\<Unavailable\>\"", "]"}]}], "]"}]}], ",",
          "\n", "  ", 
         RowBox[{"\"\<MeanSpacing\>\"", "->", 
          RowBox[{"If", "[", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"Length", "[", "gaps", "]"}], ">", "0"}], ",", 
            RowBox[{"Mean", "[", "gaps", "]"}], ",", 
            RowBox[{"Missing", "[", "\"\<NoGaps\>\"", "]"}]}], "]"}]}], ",", 
         RowBox[{"\"\<Status\>\"", "->", "status"}]}], "|>"}]}]}], "\n", 
     "]"}]}], ";"}]}]], "Input",ExpressionUUID->"73d61e7e-c74a-5949-8008-\
77da9fd138be"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"(*", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Keep", " ", "opposite"}], "-", 
     RowBox[{
     "m", " ", "and", " ", "parity", " ", "partners", " ", "separate"}]}], ",",
     " ", 
    RowBox[{"even", " ", "if", " ", "spectra", " ", 
     RowBox[{"coincide", "."}]}]}], " ", "*)"}], "\n", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"exGapRows", "[", 
     RowBox[{"results_List", ",", "p_", ",", 
      RowBox[{"window_", ":", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"1", "/", "4"}], ",", 
         RowBox[{"3", "/", "4"}]}], "}"}]}], ",", 
      RowBox[{"tol_", ":", 
       RowBox[{"10", "^", 
        RowBox[{"-", "10"}]}]}]}], "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
    RowBox[{"Flatten", "[", "\n", " ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Map", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"Function", "[", 
         RowBox[{"point", ",", 
          RowBox[{"KeyValueMap", "[", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"Function", "[", 
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{"{", 
               RowBox[{"key", ",", "s"}], "}"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
              RowBox[{"Join", "[", 
               RowBox[{
                RowBox[{"<|", 
                 RowBox[{
                  RowBox[{"\"\<L\>\"", "->", 
                   RowBox[{"p", "[", "\"\<L\>\"", "]"}]}], ",", 
                  RowBox[{"\"\<J\>\"", "->", 
                   RowBox[{"p", "[", "\"\<J\>\"", "]"}]}], ",", 
                  RowBox[{"\"\<Delta\>\"", "->", 
                   RowBox[{"p", "[", "\"\<Delta\>\"", "]"}]}], ",", "\n", 
                  "    ", 
                  RowBox[{"\"\<g\>\"", "->", 
                   RowBox[{"point", "[", "\"\<g\>\"", "]"}]}], ",", 
                  RowBox[{"\"\<gOverJ\>\"", "->", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"point", "[", "\"\<g\>\"", "]"}], "/", 
                    RowBox[{"Abs", "[", 
                    RowBox[{"p", "[", "\"\<J\>\"", "]"}], "]"}]}]}], ",", 
                  "\n", "    ", 
                  RowBox[{"\"\<SectorKey\>\"", "->", "key"}], ",", 
                  RowBox[{"\"\<Labels\>\"", "->", 
                   RowBox[{"s", "[", "\"\<Labels\>\"", "]"}]}]}], "|>"}], ",",
                 "\n", "    ", 
                RowBox[{"If", "[", 
                 RowBox[{
                  RowBox[{"TrueQ", "[", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"point", "[", "\"\<g\>\"", "]"}], "==", "0"}], 
                   "]"}], ",", "\n", "     ", 
                  RowBox[{"<|", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"\"\<SectorDimension\>\"", "->", 
                    RowBox[{"s", "[", "\"\<Dimension\>\"", "]"}]}], ",", 
                    
                    RowBox[{"\"\<Status\>\"", 
                    "->", "\"\<DecoupledEndpoint\>\""}], ",", "\n", "      ", 
                    RowBox[{"\"\<MeanR\>\"", "->", 
                    RowBox[{
                    "Missing", 
                    "[", "\"\<EndpointParentRecombinesExtraSectors\>\"", 
                    "]"}]}], ",", "\n", "      ", 
                    
                    RowBox[{"\"\<Reason\>\"", 
                    "->", "\"\<At g=0 use independently refined sectors, not \
recombined parent energies.\>\""}]}], "|>"}], ",", "\n", "     ", 
                  RowBox[{"exGapRatios", "[", 
                   RowBox[{
                    RowBox[{"s", "[", "\"\<Energies\>\"", "]"}], ",", 
                    "window", ",", "tol"}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}], 
            ",", 
            RowBox[{"point", "[", "\"\<Data\>\"", "]"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}], ",",
         "results"}], "]"}], ",", "1"}], "]"}]}], ";"}]}]], "Input",Expression\
UUID->"f117b7ce-98d1-3247-81c4-3256de5d0aed"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"(*", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Small", " ", "unjoined", " ", "markers"}], ";", " ", 
     RowBox[{"benchmarks", " ", "are", " ", "labels"}]}], ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"not", " ", "joined", " ", "reference", " ", 
     RowBox[{"curves", "."}]}]}], " ", "*)"}], "\n", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"exRatioPanel", "[", 
     RowBox[{"rows_List", ",", "labels_Association", ",", "p_", ",", 
      RowBox[{"window_", ":", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"1", "/", "4"}], ",", 
         RowBox[{"3", "/", "4"}]}], "}"}]}], ",", 
      RowBox[{"marker_", ":", "3"}]}], "]"}], " ", ":=", " ", 
    RowBox[{"Module", "[", "\n", " ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{
       "selected", ",", "valid", ",", "points", ",", "cap", ",", "g"}], "}"}],
       ",", "\n", " ", 
      RowBox[{"(*", " ", 
       RowBox[{
       "Explicit", " ", "label", " ", "matching", " ", "avoids", " ", "any", " ",
         "dependence", " ", "on", " ", "Association", " ", "key", " ", 
        RowBox[{"order", "."}]}], " ", "*)"}], "\n", " ", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"selected", "=", 
        RowBox[{"Select", "[", 
         RowBox[{"rows", ",", 
          RowBox[{"Function", "[", 
           RowBox[{"row", ",", 
            RowBox[{"And", "@@", 
             RowBox[{"KeyValueMap", "[", "\n", "   ", 
              RowBox[{
               RowBox[{
                RowBox[{
                 RowBox[{"Lookup", "[", 
                  RowBox[{
                   RowBox[{"row", "[", "\"\<Labels\>\"", "]"}], ",", "#1", ",", 
                   RowBox[{"Missing", "[", "\"\<Label\>\"", "]"}]}], "]"}], "==",
                  "#2"}], "&"}], ",", "labels"}], "]"}]}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}],
        ";", "\n", " ", 
       RowBox[{"valid", "=", 
        RowBox[{"Select", "[", 
         RowBox[{"selected", ",", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"NumericQ", "[", 
            RowBox[{"#", "[", "\"\<MeanR\>\"", "]"}], "]"}], "&"}]}], "]"}]}],
        ";", "\n", " ", 
       RowBox[{"check", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"valid", "=!=", 
          RowBox[{"{", "}"}]}], 
         ",", "\"\<This sector has no resolved gap-ratio values in the chosen \
window.\>\""}], "]"}], ";", "\n", " ", 
       RowBox[{"points", "=", 
        RowBox[{"(", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"{", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"#", "[", "\"\<gOverJ\>\"", "]"}], ",", 
             RowBox[{"#", "[", "\"\<MeanR\>\"", "]"}]}], "}"}], "&"}], " ", "/@",
           " ", "valid"}], ")"}]}], ";", "\n", " ", 
       RowBox[{"cap", "=", 
        RowBox[{"Column", "[", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"{", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"caption", "[", 
             RowBox[{"p", ",", 
              RowBox[{"\"\<\\\\Delta=\>\"", "<>", 
               RowBox[{"texNumber", "[", 
                RowBox[{"p", "[", "\"\<Delta\>\"", "]"}], "]"}]}]}], "]"}], ",",
             "\n", "   ", 
            RowBox[{"tex", "[", 
             
             RowBox[{"\"\<H_{\\\\rm \
edge}=g\\\\sum_{(i,j)\\\\in\\\\{(1,2),(L-1,L)\\\\}}(S_i^xS_j^x+S_i^yS_j^y)\>\"\
", ",", "13"}], "]"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
            RowBox[{"tex", "[", 
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{
               RowBox[{"sectorLabel", "[", "labels", "]"}], 
               "<>", "\"\<;\\\\quad d=\>\"", "<>", 
               RowBox[{"ToString", "[", 
                RowBox[{
                 RowBox[{"First", "[", "selected", "]"}], 
                 "[", "\"\<SectorDimension\>\"", "]"}], "]"}], "<>", "\n", 
               "    ", "\"\<;\\\\quad \\\\mathrm{rank\\\\ window}=[\>\"", "<>",
                "\n", "    ", 
               RowBox[{"texNumber", "[", 
                RowBox[{"window", "[", 
                 RowBox[{"[", "1", "]"}], "]"}], "]"}], "<>", "\"\<,\>\"", "<>", 
               RowBox[{"texNumber", "[", 
                RowBox[{"window", "[", 
                 RowBox[{"[", "2", "]"}], "]"}], "]"}], "<>", "\"\<]\>\""}], ",",
               "13"}], "]"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
            RowBox[{"tex", "[", 
             RowBox[{
              
              RowBox[{"\"\<\\\\langle\\\\tilde r\\\\rangle_{\\\\rm \
Poisson}=0.3863;\\\\quad \>\"", "<>", "\n", 
               "    ", "\"\<\\\\langle\\\\tilde r\\\\rangle_{\\\\rm \
GOE}\\\\simeq0.5307\>\""}], ",", "13"}], "]"}], ",", "\n", "   ", 
            RowBox[{"Style", "[", 
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{"\"\<Plotted \>\"", "<>", 
               RowBox[{"ToString", "[", 
                RowBox[{"Length", "[", "valid", "]"}], "]"}], 
               "<>", "\"\< of \>\"", "<>", 
               RowBox[{"ToString", "[", 
                RowBox[{"Length", "[", "selected", "]"}], "]"}], "<>", "\n", 
               "    ", "\"\< g samples. Excluded samples and reasons remain \
in the diagnostics table.\>\""}], ",", "12"}], "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", 
          RowBox[{"Alignment", "->", "Center"}]}], "]"}]}], ";", "\n", " ", 
       RowBox[{"g", "=", 
        RowBox[{"Block", "[", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"{", 
           RowBox[{"plotChop", "=", "0"}], "}"}], ",", 
          RowBox[{"framePlot", "[", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"{", "points", "}"}], ",", "\"\<g/|J|\>\"", 
            ",", "\"\<\\\\langle\\\\tilde r\\\\rangle\>\"", ",", "\n", "    ", 
            RowBox[{"{", "Blue", "}"}], ",", 
            RowBox[{"{", "}"}], ",", "False", ",", "False", ",", 
            RowBox[{"{", 
             RowBox[{"{", 
              RowBox[{"\"\<\[FilledCircle]\>\"", ",", "marker"}], "}"}], 
             "}"}]}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}], ";", "\n", " ", 
       RowBox[{"plotPanel", "[", 
        RowBox[{"\"\<\\\\text{Exchange: resolved-sector gap ratios}\>\"", ",",
          "cap", ",", "g"}], "]"}]}]}], "\n", "]"}]}], ";"}]}]], "Input",Expre\
ssionUUID->"a24f5eb3-12fa-ea44-a770-2090d997c74e"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["12.4 Editable gap-ratio settings and sector selection", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"9a8dbddc-8a9b-1748-a85b-0c849a6a3242"],

Cell["\<\
This selects an existing sector for display; it is not a largest-sector \
search. At the chapter-11 defaults L=10, Delta=0.5, this sector has D=71, 37 \
window levels and 35 ratios. IIDSEM is a descriptive independent-sample \
estimate; neighboring ratios and neighboring g samples are correlated. Use \
chapter 13 for independent larger-size target-sector scans.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"13c90d67-7ad7-bd4f-a2e4-a6010b41419c"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"exRatioSettings", "=", 
   RowBox[{"<|", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"\"\<RankWindow\>\"", "->", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"1", "/", "4"}], ",", 
        RowBox[{"3", "/", "4"}]}], "}"}]}], ",", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<GapResolution\>\"", "->", 
      RowBox[{"10", "^", 
       RowBox[{"-", "10"}]}]}], ",", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<MarkerSize\>\"", "->", "3"}]}], "|>"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"exRatioSector", "=", 
    RowBox[{"<|", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"\"\<m\>\"", "->", "0"}], ",", 
      RowBox[{"\"\<R\>\"", "->", "1"}], ",", 
      RowBox[{"\"\<F\>\"", "->", "1"}]}], "|>"}]}], ";"}], "   ", 
  RowBox[{"(*", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"Even", " ", "L"}], ";", " ", 
    RowBox[{"use", " ", "existing", " ", "labels", " ", "for", " ", "odd", " ", 
     RowBox[{"L", "."}]}]}], " ", "*)"}]}]}], "Input",ExpressionUUID->\
"2c3bd4c0-0bc2-c541-b014-e077c107674e"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
12.5 Compute and inspect gap-ratio diagnostics; reuse exResults\
\>", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"90666344-49aa-4749-90fd-1aec2f789952"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"check", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"ValueQ", "[", "exResults", "]"}], " ", "&&", " ", 
     RowBox[{"ValueQ", "[", "exUsed", "]"}]}], 
    ",", "\"\<Run 11.4 or load its matching results and parameters \
first.\>\""}], "]"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"exRatioSettingsUsed", "=", "exRatioSettings"}], ";", 
  RowBox[{"exRatioSectorUsed", "=", "exRatioSector"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"exGapReport", "=", 
   RowBox[{"exGapRows", "[", 
    RowBox[{"exResults", ",", "exUsed", ",", 
     RowBox[{"exRatioSettingsUsed", "[", "\"\<RankWindow\>\"", "]"}], ",", 
     "\n", " ", 
     RowBox[{"exRatioSettingsUsed", "[", "\"\<GapResolution\>\"", "]"}]}], 
    "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"exGapSelected", "=", 
   RowBox[{"Select", "[", 
    RowBox[{"exGapReport", ",", 
     RowBox[{"Function", "[", 
      RowBox[{"row", ",", 
       RowBox[{"And", "@@", 
        RowBox[{"KeyValueMap", "[", "\n", " ", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"Lookup", "[", 
             RowBox[{
              RowBox[{"row", "[", "\"\<Labels\>\"", "]"}], ",", "#1", ",", 
              RowBox[{"Missing", "[", "\"\<Label\>\"", "]"}]}], "]"}], "==", 
            "#2"}], "&"}], ",", "exRatioSectorUsed"}], "]"}]}]}], "]"}]}], 
    "]"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"check", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"exGapSelected", "=!=", 
     RowBox[{"{", "}"}]}], 
    ",", "\"\<The selected sector does not exist; inspect the labels in \
exGapReport.\>\""}], "]"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{"Dataset", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"KeyDrop", "[", 
     RowBox[{"#", ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", "\"\<Ratios\>\"", "}"}]}], "]"}], "&"}], " ", "/@", " ", 
   "exGapSelected"}], "]"}]}], "Input",ExpressionUUID->"57c54a12-6825-614e-\
b7a6-a011b73c8cac"]
}, Open  ]],

